@startuml
title collab Semantic Model — Draft

left to right direction
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
skinparam linetype ortho

class Participant {
  +name
  +kind : ParticipantKind
  +multiplicity
}

enum ParticipantKind {
  AO
  HSM
  ISR
  TIMER
}

class Collaboration {
}

class Route {
  +source : Participant
  +destination : Participant
}

class Signal {
  +name
}

abstract class Delivery

class PostDelivery {
  +queueOrder : QueueOrder
}

class PublishSubscribeDelivery
class DispatchDelivery

enum QueueOrder {
  FIFO
  LIFO
}

Participant "2" -- "0..*" Collaboration : participants
Collaboration "1" *-- "1..*" Route : routes

Participant "1" <-- "0..*" Route : source
Participant "1" <-- "0..*" Route : destination

Signal "1" <-- "1..*" Route : signal
Delivery "1" <-- "1..*" Route : delivery

Delivery <|-- PostDelivery
Delivery <|-- PublishSubscribeDelivery
Delivery <|-- DispatchDelivery

PostDelivery --> QueueOrder

note right of Participant
A Participant is a semantic system role/classifier.
Multiplicity records the anticipated runtime population.
end note

note bottom of Route
Delivery semantics belong to each Route,
not to Signal identity.
end note

note right of Delivery
POST is queued delivery to an AO.
PUBLISH/SUBSCRIBE is framework-routed delivery.
DISPATCH is synchronous delivery to a passive HSM.
end note

@enduml
